    "content": "Nicola is a name of Greek origin, derived from Nikolaos, meaning \"victory of the people\" (nikē for victory, laos for people). Commonly used as a female first name in English-speaking countries and Italian (often male), it signifies strength and triumph. Famous examples include actresses Nicola Peltz and Nicola Walker. Key Details About the Name Nicola: Meaning: \"Victory of the people\". Origin: Greek (via Latin). Gender: Primarily female, but historically and in Italian, it is a male name. Nicknames: Nicky, Nikki, Nic. Famous People: Nicola Peltz Beckham: American actress (Transformers: Age of Extinction). Nicola Walker: English actress (Spooks, Unforgotten). Nicola Coughlan: Irish actress (Bridgerton, Derry Girls). Common Last Names: Common pairings include English or Italian surnames such as Smith, Jones, Rossi, or Bianchi. Other Contexts: Nicola is also a popular Japanese fashion magazine for teenage girls.",
